# Cloudflare Pages - caching rules. More specific paths win.
#
# NOTE: we deliberately do NOT define a catch-all `/*` Cache-Control rule.
# Cloudflare Pages already serves HTML with `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`
# by default (and purges the edge cache on every deploy), so a `/*` rule is
# redundant for HTML - and worse, Pages MERGES matching rules, so a `/*` rule
# would concatenate into `/videos/*` producing a malformed double Cache-Control
# (two max-age values). That stops the edge from caching the video, which forces
# a permanent cache MISS where Cloudflare returns the whole file as 200 and never
# serves HTTP range (206) requests - breaking in-video seeking. Keeping the
# video header single + cacheable lets the edge serve 206 so users can seek
# (travel) to any point in the video instantly.

# Security headers on every response. Deliberately a separate block from the
# Cache-Control rules above (and using different header names) so it can't hit
# the Cache-Control merge bug described above - these never collide with the
# /videos/* or /images/* Cache-Control values.
#
# Content-Security-Policy here intentionally carries ONLY frame-ancestors:
# the CSP spec ignores frame-ancestors when delivered via <meta>, so it can't
# live in astro.config.mjs's `security.csp` like the rest of the policy does.
# script-src/style-src/base-uri/form-action/etc. are set per-page by Astro's
# auto-hashed <meta> CSP (see astro.config.mjs) - duplicating them here with
# a non-hashed 'self' would make this header's script-src the operative
# (more restrictive, hash-less) one and break every inline script Astro emits.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains; preload
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=()
  Content-Security-Policy: frame-ancestors 'none'

# Astro's build output is content-hashed → safe to cache forever.
/_astro/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Self-hosted media: cache a day, revalidate after.
/images/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, must-revalidate

# Self-hosted videos: cacheable so the edge serves 206 range requests (seeking).
/videos/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, must-revalidate
  Accept-Ranges: bytes
